{"chunk_id": "04279ab37556", "text": "Rama, devastated by Sita\u2019s abduction, erupts into a cosmic fury. Declaring that if he does not recover her he will unleash every weapon of destruction, he prepares himself like a god of annihilation\u2014tightening his bark garments, taking up his bow, and resembling Rudra poised to destroy the triple cities. His wrath grows so immense that he threatens to destroy the entire universe\u2014gods, spirits, humans, serpents, and mountains alike. Lakshmana, terrified at seeing a rage never before shown by his brother, steps forward with folded hands to restrain him. He reminds Rama of his true nature: gentle, self-controlled, and devoted to the welfare of all beings. Lakshmana argues that the sin of a single wrongdoer should not lead to the destruction of the worlds, appealing to Rama\u2019s divine restraint and moral greatness.\nRama, enraged by Sita\u2019s abduction, vows to destroy the universe, but Lakshmana respectfully pleads with him to restrain his wrath.\nThemes: righteous anger, brotherly counsel, self-control vs wrath, cosmic destruction imagery", "vector": [0.010183663107454777, -0.02892947383224964, 0.001930214581079781, 0.007951534353196621, -0.01738210767507553, 0.016052329912781715, -0.03424858674407005, -0.015102487988770008, -0.013582739979028702, -0.02418026328086853, 0.008148287422955036, 0.008596070110797882, 0.01531959418207407, 0.016513681039214134, 0.01135739590972662, 0.010807844810187817, 0.04719357565045357, -0.013738785870373249, 0.038590721786022186, 0.0005503995344042778, -0.0001343135954812169, -0.015590977855026722, -0.008813176304101944, -0.002623938489705324, -0.027952492237091064, -0.012978912331163883, 0.024275247007608414, -0.03924204409122467, 0.02264694683253765, -0.006557302083820105, -0.010054755955934525, -0.01811484433710575, 0.003387204371392727, -0.0013925362145528197, -0.01782989129424095, 0.009593403898179531, 0.005885628052055836, -0.012544699013233185, -0.00427768100053072, -0.025